8	> You connect this server to your MCP client at your own responsibility. Language models can make mistakes, misinterpret instructions, or perform unintended actions. Review tool outputs, verify changes (e.g., with `search_events`), and prefer small, incremental writes.
9	>
10	> The HTTP/OAuth layer is designed for convenience during development, not production-grade security. If deploying remotely, harden it: proper token validation, secure storage, TLS termination, strict CORS/origin checks, rate limiting, audit logging, and compliance with Google's terms.
11	
12	## Notice
13	
14	This repo works in two ways:
15	- As a **Node/Hono server** for local workflows
16	- As a **Cloudflare Worker** for remote interactions
17	
18	For production Cloudflare deployments, see [Remote Model Context Protocol servers (MCP)](https://blog.cloudflare.com/remote-model-context-protocol-servers-mcp).
19	
20	## Features
21	
22	- ✅ **Events** — Search across ALL calendars, create, update, delete, respond to invitations
23	- ✅ **Calendars** — Discover available calendars
24	- ✅ **Availability** — Check free/busy status before scheduling
25	- ✅ **Natural Language** — Create events with text like "Lunch tomorrow at noon"
26	- ✅ **Google Meet** — Auto-create Meet links for events
27	- ✅ **OAuth 2.1** — Secure PKCE flow with RS token mapping
28	- ✅ **Dual Runtime** — Node.js/Bun or Cloudflare Workers
29	
30	### Design Principles
31	
32	- **LLM-friendly**: Tools are simplified and unified, not 1:1 API mirrors
33	- **Smart defaults**: Search all calendars, no notification spam, recurring expansion
34	- **Just works**: `search_events` searches all calendars by default — no setup needed
35	- **Clear feedback**: Every response includes which calendar each event belongs to
36	- **Limited features**: Due to the model's hallucinations, tools for managing calendars are not included. Ensure that you use the client that allows you to confirm dangerous actions, such as event deletion or updating.
37	
38	---
39	
40	## Installation
41	
42	Prerequisites: [Bun](https://bun.sh/), [Node.js 20+](https://nodejs.org), [Google Cloud](https://console.cloud.google.com) project. For remote: a [Cloudflare](https://dash.cloudflare.com) account.
43	
44	### Ways to Run (Pick One)
45	
46	1. **Local + OAuth** — Standard setup with Google OAuth
47	2. **Cloudflare Worker (wrangler dev)** — Local Worker testing
48	3. **Cloudflare Worker (deploy)** — Remote production
49	
50	---
51	
52	### 1. Local + OAuth — Quick Start
53	
54	1. Set up Google Cloud Console:
55	
56	   **Create Project & Enable API:**
57	   - Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com)
58	   - Create a new project (or select existing)
59	   - Navigate to **APIs & Services > Library**
60	   - Search for "Google Calendar API" and click **Enable**
61	
62	   **Configure OAuth Consent Screen** (required before credentials):
63	   - Go to **APIs & Services > OAuth consent screen**
64	   - Select **External** (or Internal for Workspace)
65	   - Fill in app name, user support email, developer email
66	   - Add scopes: `../auth/calendar.events`, `../auth/calendar.readonly`
67	   - Add your email as a **Test user** (required while app is in "Testing" mode)
68	   - Save
69	
70	   **Create Credentials:**
71	   - Go to **APIs & Services > Credentials**
72	   - Click **Create Credentials > OAuth client ID**
73	   - Application type: **Web application**
74	   - Name: anything (e.g., "Google Calendar MCP")
75	   - Authorized redirect URIs: `http://127.0.0.1:3001/oauth/callback`
76	   - Click **Create** and copy **Client ID** and **Client Secret**
77	
78	2. Configure environment:
79	
80	```bash
81	git clone <repo>
82	cd google-calendar-mcp
83	bun install
84	cp env.example .env
85	```
86	
87	Edit `.env`:
88	
89	```env
90	PORT=3000
91	AUTH_ENABLED=true
92	
93	PROVIDER_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
94	PROVIDER_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret
95	
96	OAUTH_SCOPES=https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
97	OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:3001/oauth/callback
98	OAUTH_REDIRECT_ALLOWLIST=alice://oauth/callback,http://127.0.0.1:3001/oauth/callback
99	```
100	
101	3. Run:
102	
103	```bash
104	bun dev
105	# MCP: http://127.0.0.1:3000/mcp
106	# OAuth: http://127.0.0.1:3001
107	```
108	
109	> **Tip:** The Authorization Server runs on PORT+1 (3001 by default).
110	
111	**Claude Desktop / Cursor:**
112	
113	```json
114	{
115	  "mcpServers": {
116	    "google-calendar": {
117	      "command": "bunx",
118	      "args": ["mcp-remote", "http://localhost:3000/mcp", "--transport", "http-only"],
119	      "env": { "NO_PROXY": "127.0.0.1,localhost" }
120	    }
121	  }
122	}
123	```
124	
125	#### Token Encryption (Recommended)
126	
127	Generate an encryption key for secure token storage:
128	
129	```bash
130	openssl rand -base64 32
131	```
132	
133	Add to `.env`:
134	
135	```env
136	RS_TOKENS_ENC_KEY=your-32-byte-base64-key
137	```
138	
