140	
141	### 2. Cloudflare Worker (Local Dev)
142	
143	```bash
144	bun x wrangler dev --local | cat
145	```
146	
147	With OAuth:
148	
149	```bash
150	bun x wrangler secret put PROVIDER_CLIENT_ID
151	bun x wrangler secret put PROVIDER_CLIENT_SECRET
152	bun x wrangler dev --local | cat
153	```
154	
155	Endpoint: `http://127.0.0.1:8787/mcp`
156	
157	---
158	
159	### 3. Cloudflare Worker (Deploy)
160	
161	1. Create KV namespace for token storage:
162	
163	```bash
164	bun x wrangler kv:namespace create TOKENS
165	```
166	
167	Output will show:
168	```
169	Add the following to your wrangler.toml:
170	[[kv_namespaces]]
171	binding = "TOKENS"
172	id = "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
173	```
174	
175	2. Update `wrangler.toml` with your KV namespace ID:
176	
177	```toml
178	[[kv_namespaces]]
179	binding = "TOKENS"
180	id = "your-kv-namespace-id-from-step-1"
181	```
182	
183	3. Set secrets:
184	
185	```bash
186	bun x wrangler secret put PROVIDER_CLIENT_ID
187	bun x wrangler secret put PROVIDER_CLIENT_SECRET
188	
189	# Generate encryption key (32-byte base64url):
190	openssl rand -base64 32 | tr -d '=' | tr '+/' '-_'
191	bun x wrangler secret put TOKENS_ENC_KEY
192	```
193	
194	> **Note:** `TOKENS_ENC_KEY` encrypts OAuth tokens stored in KV (AES-256-GCM). Without it, tokens are stored unencrypted!
195	
196	4. Update redirect URI in `wrangler.toml`:
197	
198	```toml
199	OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI = "https://your-worker.your-subdomain.workers.dev/oauth/callback"
200	OAUTH_REDIRECT_ALLOWLIST = "alice://oauth/callback,https://your-worker.your-subdomain.workers.dev/oauth/callback"
201	```
202	
203	5. Add Workers URL to your Google Cloud OAuth app's redirect URIs
204	
205	6. Deploy:
206	
207	```bash
208	bun x wrangler deploy
209	```
210	
211	Endpoint: `https://<worker-name>.<account>.workers.dev/mcp`
212	
