215	## Client Configuration
216	
217	### Pre-authenticate (Recommended)
218	
219	Claude Desktop has short timeouts that can kill the OAuth flow mid-process. **Pre-authenticate manually first:**
220	
221	```bash
222	
223	# Authenticate (complete Google sign-in when browser opens)
224	npx mcp-remote https://your-worker.workers.dev/mcp --transport http-only
225	```
226	
227	Once you see "Authentication successful!", tokens are cached and Claude Desktop will use them.
228	
229	### Claude Desktop / Cursor (Local Server)
230	
231	```json
232	{
233	  "mcpServers": {
234	    "google-calendar": {
235	      "command": "npx",
236	      "args": ["mcp-remote", "http://127.0.0.1:3000/mcp", "--transport", "http-only"],
237	      "env": { "NO_PROXY": "127.0.0.1,localhost" }
238	    }
239	  }
240	}
241	```
242	
243	### Claude Desktop / Cursor (Cloudflare Worker)
244	
245	```json
246	{
247	  "mcpServers": {
248	    "google-calendar": {
249	      "command": "npx",
250	      "args": ["mcp-remote", "https://your-worker.workers.dev/mcp", "--transport", "http-only"]
251	    }
252	  }
253	}
254	```
255	
256	### Node Version Issues (nvm users)
257	
258	If you get `ReadableStream is not defined` or similar errors, Claude Desktop may be using an old Node version. Fix by specifying the full path:
259	
260	```json
261	{
262	  "mcpServers": {
263	    "google-calendar": {
264	      "command": "/Users/YOUR_USER/.nvm/versions/node/v22.0.0/bin/npx",
265	      "args": ["mcp-remote", "https://your-worker.workers.dev/mcp", "--transport", "http-only"],
266	      "env": {
267	        "PATH": "/Users/YOUR_USER/.nvm/versions/node/v22.0.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"
268	      }
269	    }
270	  }
271	}
272	```
273	
274	Find your node path with: `which node`
