1	# Docs.rs MCP Server
2	
3	[![License: Apache 2.0](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-Apache%202.0-yellow.svg?style=for-the-badge?logo=apache)](https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0)
4	
5	>A **Model Context Protocol** (MCP) server for **fetching Rust crate documentation** from [docs.rs](https://docs.rs)
6	
7	[Features](#features) • [Getting Started](#getting-started) • [Tools](#tools) • [Contributing](#contributing) • [Acknowledgments](#acknowledgments) • [License](#license)
8	
9	## Features
10	<a id="features"></a>
11	
12	- **Find New Crates** - Search crates by exact name, partial match, or fuzzy query to discover relevant libraries
13	- **Inspect Crate Symbols** - Inspect structs, traits, functions, and any other symbol inside a crate
14	- **Review Crate Summaries** - Get a crate overview with its structure and public API surface
15	- **Read Full Documentation** - Read crate-level documentation
16	
17	## Getting Started
18	<a id="getting-started"></a>
19	
20	### Using Pre-built Executables
21	
22	Download the latest release for your platform from the [Releases](https://github.com/vexxvakan/mcp-docsrs/releases) page:
23	
24	#### Linux
25	
26	- **x64/AMD64 (GLIBC)**: `mcp-docsrs-linux-x64` - For Ubuntu, Debian, Fedora, etc.
27	- **ARM64 (GLIBC)**: `mcp-docsrs-linux-arm64` - For ARM64 systems, AWS Graviton
28	- **x64/AMD64 (MUSL)**: `mcp-docsrs-linux-x64-musl` - For Alpine Linux, Docker containers (requires libstdc++)
29	- **ARM64 (MUSL)**: `mcp-docsrs-linux-arm64-musl` - For Alpine on ARM64, minimal containers (requires libstdc++)
30	
31	#### macOS
32	
33	- **Intel**: `mcp-docsrs-darwin-x64` - For Intel-based Macs
34	- **Apple Silicon**: `mcp-docsrs-darwin-arm64` - For M-series Macs
35	
36	#### Windows
37	
38	- **x64**: `mcp-docsrs-windows-x64.exe` - For 64-bit Windows
39	
40	### Using Docker
41	
42	Pull and run the latest multi-arch image (supports both x64 and ARM64):
43	
44	```bash
45	# Pull the latest image
46	docker pull ghcr.io/vexxvakan/mcp-docsrs:latest
47	
48	# Run the server
49	docker run --rm -i ghcr.io/vexxvakan/mcp-docsrs:latest
50	
51	# Run with custom configuration
52	docker run --rm -i ghcr.io/vexxvakan/mcp-docsrs:latest \
53	  --cache-ttl 7200000 --max-cache-size 200
54	```
55	
56	Available tags:
57	
58	- `latest` - Latest stable release (multi-arch)
59	- `v1.0.0` - Specific version (multi-arch)
60	
61	### MCP Setup
62	
63	| Client | Command |
64	| ---------- | ---------- |
65	| Codex | `codex mcp add docsrs -- path/to/mcp-docsrs` |
66	| Claude Code | `claude mcp add --transport stdio docsrs -- path/to/mcp-docsrs` |
67	| Gemini CLI | `gemini mcp add -s user docsrs path/to/mcp-docsrs` |
68	| OpenCode | Run `opencode mcp add`, choose a local MCP server, then point it at `path/to/mcp-docsrs`. |
69	| VS Code | Open Command Palette (`Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+P`) → `MCP: Add Server` → choose `Workspace` or `User` → `Command (stdio)` → enter `path/to/mcp-docsrs`. |
70	| Cursor | Open Settings (`Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+J`) → `Tools & Integrations` → `New MCP Server` → choose a local/stdio server → enter `path/to/mcp-docsrs`. |
71	
72	After adding the server, restart the client if it does not discover the tools immediately.
73	
74	### Configuration
75	
76	Configure the server using environment variables or command-line arguments:
77	
78	| Variable | CLI Flag | Default | Description |
79	| ---------- | ---------- | --------- | ------------- |
80	| `CACHE_TTL` | `--cache-ttl` | 3600000 | Cache time-to-live in milliseconds |
81	| `MAX_CACHE_SIZE` | `--max-cache-size` | 100 | Maximum number of cached entries |
82	| `REQUEST_TIMEOUT` | `--request-timeout` | 30000 | HTTP request timeout in milliseconds |
83	| `DB_PATH` | `--db-path` | :memory: | Path to SQLite database file |
84	
85	## Tools
86	<a id="tools"></a>
87	
88	The server exposes four MCP tools:
89	
90	### Crate
91	
92	#### `crate_lookup`
93	
94	Retrieves a crate overview with its structure and public API surface from docs.rs.
95	
96	| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
97	| ---------- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------- |
98	| `crateName` | string | Yes | Name of the Rust crate to inspect |
99	| `version` | string | No | Specific version or semver range, for example `"1.0.0"` or `"~4"` |
100	| `target` | string | No | Target platform, for example `"i686-pc-windows-msvc"` |
101	| `formatVersion` | number | No | Rustdoc JSON format version |
102	
103	```json
104	{
105	  "tool": "crate_lookup",
106	  "arguments": {
107	    "crateName": "tokio",
108	    "version": "1.48.0"
109	  }
110	}
111	```
112	
113	#### `crate_docs`
114	
115	Retrieves the crate-level documentation page from docs.rs.
116	
117	| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
118	| ---------- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------- |
119	| `crateName` | string | Yes | Name of the Rust crate to inspect |
120	| `version` | string | No | Specific version or semver range, for example `"1.0.0"` or `"~4"` |
121	| `target` | string | No | Target platform, for example `"i686-pc-windows-msvc"` |
122	| `formatVersion` | number | No | Rustdoc JSON format version |
123	
124	```json
125	{
126	  "tool": "crate_docs",
127	  "arguments": {
128	    "crateName": "serde"
129	  }
130	}
131	```
132	
133	#### `crate_find`
134	
135	Searches crates.io for matching crates and returns ranked results using fuzzy and partial name matching.
136	
137	| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
138	| ---------- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------- |
139	| `query` | string | Yes | Search query for crate names |
140	| `limit` | number | No | Maximum number of results to return. Defaults to `10` |
141	
142	```json
143	{
144	  "tool": "crate_find",
145	  "arguments": {
146	    "query": "rustdoc json",
147	    "limit": 5
148	  }
149	}
150	```
151	
152	### Symbol
153	
154	#### `symbol_lookup`
155	
156	Retrieves structured symbol metadata for one symbol inside a crate.
157	
158	| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
159	| ---------- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------- |
160	| `crateName` | string | Yes | Name of the Rust crate |
161	| `symbolType` | string | Yes | Rustdoc symbol type, for example `"struct"`, `"function"`, or `"trait"` |
162	| `symbolname` | string | Yes | Symbol name or path, for example `"runtime::Runtime"` or `"spawn"` |
163	| `version` | string | No | Specific version or semver range |
164	| `target` | string | No | Target platform |
165	
166	```json
167	{
168	  "tool": "symbol_lookup",
169	  "arguments": {
170	    "crateName": "tokio",
171	    "symbolType": "struct",
172	    "symbolname": "runtime::Runtime"
173	  }
174	}
175	```
176	
177	#### `symbol_docs`
178	
179	Retrieves the full documentation body for one symbol inside a crate.
180	
181	| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
182	| ---------- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------- |
183	| `crateName` | string | Yes | Name of the Rust crate |
184	| `symbolType` | string | Yes | Rustdoc symbol type, for example `"struct"`, `"function"`, or `"trait"` |
185	| `symbolname` | string | Yes | Symbol name or path, for example `"runtime::Runtime"` or `"spawn"` |
186	| `version` | string | No | Specific version or semver range |
187	| `target` | string | No | Target platform |
188	
189	```json
190	{
191	  "tool": "symbol_docs",
192	  "arguments": {
193	    "crateName": "tokio",
194	    "symbolType": "struct",
195	    "symbolname": "runtime::Runtime"
196	  }
197	}
198	```
